tests/isla/m7-traces.sh traces the Thumb forms of LeanExe/M7/Machine.lean from armv9p4-t32.ir, which
this diff makes from armv9p4-checked.ir, armv9p4.ir with tests/isla/armv9p4-checked.diff applied.
The diff appends two harness functions, isla_footprint_t32 for a 32-bit opcode and
isla_footprint_t16 for a 16-bit one, and changes nothing else.  Each does what
isla_footprint_no_init and isla_footprint_common do for an A64 opcode (isla_main.sail 51-73): it
runs InitFeatureImpl, sets SEE to -1 and DBGEN to Signal_Low, runs Isla's reset, sets __ThisInstr
and __ThisInstrEnc, and marks the start of the trace with check_cycle_count.  It then sets
__currentCond, which __InstructionExecute sets through __SetThisInstrDetails with __DefaultCond
(fetch.sail 299), and calls __DecodeExecute (fetch.sail 250), which decodes and executes the
instruction through ExecuteT32__1 or ExecuteT16 and retries the decode once after an SEE
exception.  Around that call it keeps the handler of armv9p4-checked.ir: Error_ExceptionTaken
ends the path normally, and every other exception fails a Sail assertion, which ends Isla's run
with an error.

__DefaultCond gives AL outside an IT block, and the decode of B T3 tests ConditionPassed(), which
reads __currentCond, and never the cond field of its opcode (instrs32.sail 1463-1476), so with
__InstructionExecute's setting the Sail model branches on every B<cond>.W outside an IT block.
CurrentCond() of DDI 0403E.e A7.3.1 returns the cond field of the encoding for the T1 and T3
encodings of B and ITSTATE's condition otherwise.  isla_footprint_t32 follows it: an opcode whose
bits 31 to 27, 15, 14, and 12 are 11110, 1, 0, and 0 and whose bits 25 to 23 are not 111, the
pattern of B T3 (instrs32.sail 1478), gets bits 25 to 22 as its condition, and every other opcode
gets __DefaultCond(__T32).  isla_footprint_t16 sets __DefaultCond(__T16); the only 16-bit form of
the model, BX, is not B T1.  The condition's computation and its write follow the cycle event, so
a trace records them, while Isla drops the writes that come before it.  Apply with
`cp armv9p4-checked.ir armv9p4-t32.ir && patch armv9p4-t32.ir < armv9p4-t32.diff`.

